# Styles Package (`packages/styles/`)

Publishable PDS style libraries covering multiple styling targets, plus a local demo app for preview.

## Structure

```
packages/styles/
├── projects/
│   ├── global-styles/       # Global CSS package (@porsche-design-system/global-styles)
│   ├── tailwindcss/         # Tailwind CSS plugin (@porsche-design-system/tailwindcss)
│   ├── scss/                # SCSS mixins/variables (@porsche-design-system/scss)
│   ├── emotion/             # Emotion helpers (@porsche-design-system/emotion)
│   └── vanilla-extract/     # Vanilla Extract theme (@porsche-design-system/vanilla-extract)
├── src/                     # Demo app / local preview UI (NOT the published library)
├── tests/
│   └── vrt/                 # Visual regression tests
└── shared/                  # Shared style source consumed by sub-packages
```

## Key Distinction

- `projects/*` — source of truth for publishable style packages
- `src/` — demo application and preview surface, **not** the published output
- `dist/` — generated output, do not edit

## Working Guidelines

- Make changes in the relevant style target package (`projects/*`), not just the demo
- Keep naming and token usage aligned across style targets unless a package intentionally exposes a target-specific API
- Cross-target changes (e.g., a shared token helper) may affect several style packages at once — verify all affected packages
- Token values come from `@porsche-design-system/tokens` — import from there, don't hardcode
- Each sub-package has its own build, test, and publish configuration

## Style Targets

| Package | Purpose | Usage |
|---------|---------|-------|
| `global-styles` | CSS custom properties + reset | `@import '@porsche-design-system/global-styles'` |
| `tailwindcss` | Tailwind CSS plugin with PDS tokens | `@plugin '@porsche-design-system/tailwindcss'` |
| `scss` | SCSS variables and mixins | `@use '@porsche-design-system/scss'` |
| `emotion` | Emotion CSS-in-JS helpers | `import { ... } from '@porsche-design-system/emotion'` |
| `vanilla-extract` | Vanilla Extract theme | `import { ... } from '@porsche-design-system/vanilla-extract'` |

## Downstream Impact

Style changes affect components and all consumers:

```
tokens → styles → components → components-js → wrappers → storefront
```

## Testing

- Run unit tests for the specific subpackage you change
- Run `npm run test:vrt:styles` when visual contracts or rendered demo output changes
- Be careful with cross-target changes — they may affect multiple packages

## Commands

```bash
npm run build:styles                   # Build all style packages + demo
npm run test:unit:styles               # Unit tests for all
npm run test:unit:styles:shared-styles # Unit tests for shared styles only
npm run test:vrt:styles                # VRT tests
npm run build:styles:tailwindcss       # Build only Tailwind package
npm run build:styles:scss              # Build only SCSS package
npm run build:styles:emotion           # Build only Emotion package
npm run build:styles:vanilla-extract   # Build only Vanilla Extract package
npm run build:styles:global-styles     # Build only Global Styles package
```
